1
00:00:08,536 --> 00:00:14,476
A fork is a catalogue game adapted for your course.

2
00:00:14,536 --> 00:00:22,063
The scientific model and the server verification stay the same, so every student progresses on the same trusted measure.

3
00:00:22,673 --> 00:00:25,543
It all starts on the Partners page.

4
00:00:25,603 --> 00:00:30,343
Three steps: add your institution, fork a game, share it by QR.

5
00:00:30,403 --> 00:00:36,300
The questions below explain what you can change in a fork.

6
00:00:36,910 --> 00:00:45,790
Step 1: add your institution. A name, a short description and a logo are enough.

7
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:55,110
You apply with your institutional email address, and the university team verifies the domain.

8
00:00:55,170 --> 00:01:00,707
In this video we use an example institution created for the demo.

9
00:01:01,317 --> 00:01:06,657
Once verified, your institution page shows the “Verified partner” badge.

10
00:01:06,717 --> 00:01:11,387
Step 2: a new joint game. Choose the game and the level range.

11
00:01:11,447 --> 00:01:18,657
Write the title, the course name and an introduction for your students.

12
00:01:18,717 --> 00:01:25,114
Press “Fork and create”: the game is published under both logos.

13
00:01:25,724 --> 00:01:30,394
The joint game has its own page: your logo next to İDÜ’s seal.

14
00:01:30,454 --> 00:01:37,864
The levels and the lineage are on the same page. A green tick means the signature was just re-verified.

15
00:01:37,924 --> 00:01:43,419
Inside the game, a strip with both logos stays on top.

16
00:01:44,029 --> 00:01:51,389
Step 3: share. One click gives a print-ready A4 poster with a QR code.

17
00:01:51,449 --> 00:01:57,289
Or run a live class straight from the joint game.

18
00:01:57,349 --> 00:02:01,724
Students join without an account, using a nickname.

19
00:02:02,334 --> 00:02:05,254
A fork can be forked too.

20
00:02:05,314 --> 00:02:21,154
Example High School adapts the university’s workshop for Grade 11.

21
00:02:21,214 --> 00:02:26,554
The new page shows where it came from: “Forked from Example University”.

22
00:02:26,614 --> 00:02:30,198
The source of the work never disappears.

23
00:02:30,808 --> 00:02:34,548
The lineage ledger: who forked what, from where?

24
00:02:34,608 --> 00:02:43,548
Each block carries the SHA-256 hash of the one before it and is signed with Ed25519: it cannot be deleted or silently changed.

25
00:02:43,608 --> 00:02:50,537
The ledger holds no personal data, only identifiers and content hashes.

26
00:02:51,347 --> 00:03:04,775
Free, with no contract: an open education project of Izmir Demokrasi University.

